/*  The checker's walk over a program — `TypeChecker.Check` in `src/Interpreter/TypeChecker.Core.cs`.

    A judgement gives back `void or failure` (or `node or failure`, for a type): nothing when all is
    well, or a failure whose message is `error\t` and the C# checker's words, or `unsupported\t`
    and what this checker met that it cannot judge yet.

    ★ A type is a tree node, the same kind the parser builds for an annotation — `(NumberType)`,
    `(SeriesType (TextType))`. One the checker cannot work out is a node of kind `none`, which is
    what C# means by a null type: not a refusal, just nothing to go on.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// What a name stands for in a scope — C#'s `TypeInfo`.
    Define object binding with (the node shape, the node established-by, the number line, the fact permanent,
        the fact module, the number depth, the fact parameter).

    Define object checker with (
        the series of map from text to binding scopes,
        the map from text to number ended-names,
        the map from text to fact hoisted-constants,
        the map from text to node narrowed,
        the fact in-function,
        the series of node expected-returns,
        the number function-line,
        the map from text to fact hidden,
        the map from text to node defs,
        the series of text def-order,
        the map from text to fact templates,
        the map from text to fact bundled,
        the series of map from text to node type-scopes,
        the number rabbit-depth,
        the number nesting,
        the map from text to node untos,
        the series of text unto-order,
        the fact in-try,
        the fact handled,
        the fact in-exception-handler,
        the map from text to node interfaces,
        the text checking-module,
        the map from text to series of text module-needs,
        the series of pending-pull pending-pulls).

    /// A pull of a module, remembered with the names visible at it — its needs are verified once
    /// every module's body has been checked, since one may be defined after the block that pulls it.
    Define object pending-pull with (the text module, the number line, the series of text visible).

    Bind node to unknown-type:
        Return cast shaped on ("none").
    Done.

    /// Two types the same — structurally, and an object type by its name alone.
    Bind fact to same-type, given (the node first, the node second):
        Return cast type-key on (first) is cast type-key on (second).
    Done.

    /// A type's identity as text: an object type by its name, a function type by its parameter and
    /// return types — not by what its parameters are called.
    Bind text to type-key, given (the node shape):
        If shape's kind is "atom", return shape's word.
        If shape's kind is "ObjectType", return "(ObjectType {(cast field-of on (shape, 1))'s word})".
        Define out as a chase.
        Insert "(" into out.
        Insert shape's kind into out.
        Define place as 0.
        For each inner in shape's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If shape's kind is not "FunctionType" or place is less than 3:
                Insert " " into out.
                Insert cast type-key on (inner) into out.
            Done.
        Done.
        Insert ")" into out.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.

    // ── Scopes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `(VariableReference "name" 0 0)` — what a name no statement wrote is established by.
    Bind node to named-reference, given (the text name):
        Return cast made on ("VariableReference", a series with (cast quoted on (name), cast numeral on (0), cast numeral on (0))).
    Done.

    /// The scope every program starts in, and every function body: `input` and `output`.
    Bind map from text to binding to builtin-scope:
        Define reading as cast shaped on ("ReadableStreamType").
        Cast reading's add on (cast plain-type on ("TextType")).
        Define writing as cast shaped on ("WritableStreamType").
        Cast writing's add on (cast plain-type on ("TextType")).
        Define scope as a map from text to binding.
        In scope, the entry for "input" becomes a new binding {
            the shape reading, the established-by cast named-reference on ("input"), the line 0, the permanent false, the module false, the depth 0, the parameter false }.
        In scope, the entry for "output" becomes a new binding {
            the shape writing, the established-by cast named-reference on ("output"), the line 0, the permanent false, the module false, the depth 0, the parameter false }.
        Return scope.
    Done.

    Bind map from text to binding to innermost unto checker:
        Return item (the number of one's scopes) of one's scopes.
    Done.

    Bind void to enter-scope unto checker:
        Insert a map from text to binding into one's scopes.
        Insert a map from text to node into one's type-scopes.
    Done.

    /// Leaving a block remembers what it held, to tell "never defined" from "its block ended".
    Bind void to exit-scope unto checker:
        Define leaving as cast one's innermost.
        For each pair in leaving, repeat:
            Define held as the value of pair.
            If held's line is greater than 0:
                In one's ended-names, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes held's line.
            Done.
        Done.
        Remove item (the number of one's scopes) from one's scopes.
        Remove item (the number of one's type-scopes) from one's type-scopes.
    Done.

    /// The binding a name has here, innermost first — or void.
    Bind voidable binding to look-up unto checker, given (the text name):
        Define depth as the number of one's scopes.
        While depth is greater than 0, repeat:
            Define found as the entry for name in item depth of one's scopes.
            If found is not void, return found.
            Decrement depth by 1.
        Done.
        Return void.
    Done.

    /// The same, skipping the innermost scope.
    Bind voidable binding to look-up-outer unto checker, given (the text name):
        Define depth as the number of one's scopes - 1.
        While depth is greater than 0, repeat:
            Define found as the entry for name in item depth of one's scopes.
            If found is not void, return found.
            Decrement depth by 1.
        Done.
        Return void.
    Done.

    Bind void to bind-name unto checker, given (the text name, the binding held):
        Define here as cast one's innermost.
        In here, the entry for name becomes held.
    Done.

    // ── Books ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// A book bundled with the language — `BuiltinBooks`.
    Bind fact to is-a-book, given (the text name):
        Define lowered as name in lowercase.
        For each book in a series with ("math", "collections", "blueprints", "chance", "c-language", "cufet", "regex"), repeat:
            If lowered is book, return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// The bundled book that introduces this type name, or "".
    Bind text to book-introducing, given (the text name):
        Define lowered as name in lowercase.
        If lowered is "matrix" or lowered is "chase", return "collections".
        If lowered is "step" or lowered is "pin", return "blueprints".
        Return "".
    Done.

    // ── What this checker can judge ───────────────────────────────────────

    /// The first statement kind, anywhere in the program, this checker cannot judge yet — or "".
    /// ⚠ Asked of the WHOLE program before anything is checked, because the C# checker gathers
    /// declarations first: a refusal it gives while hoisting comes before any in the statements.
    Bind text to beyond-reach, given (the node statements):
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            Define inner as cast statement-beyond-reach on (statement).
            If inner is not "", return inner.
        Done.
        Return "".
    Done.

    Bind text to statement-beyond-reach, given (the node statement):
        Define kind as statement's kind.
        If kind is "DefineStatement":
            Define declared as cast field-of on (statement, 7).
            If cast is-nothing on (declared) is false:
                If cast beyond-types on (declared) or declared's kind is "AxiomType" or declared's kind is "AddressType":
                    Return "a Define declared as {declared's kind}".
                Done.
            Done.
            If the number of statement's children is greater than 7, return "a Define given parameters".
            Return "".
        Done.
        If kind is "IfStatement":
            For each arm in (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s children, repeat:
                Define inner as cast beyond-reach on (cast field-of on (arm, 2)).
                If inner is not "", return inner.
            Done.
            Define otherwise-body as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
            If cast is-nothing on (otherwise-body), return "".
            Return cast beyond-reach on (otherwise-body).
        Done.
        If kind is "JudgeStatement":
            For each arm in (cast field-of on (statement, 2))'s children, repeat:
                Define inner as cast beyond-reach on (cast field-of on (arm, 2)).
                If inner is not "", return inner.
            Done.
            Define rest as cast field-of on (statement, 3).
            If cast is-nothing on (rest), return "".
            Return cast beyond-reach on (rest).
        Done.
        If kind is "WhileStatement", return cast beyond-reach on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)).
        If kind is "WithOpenStatement", return cast beyond-reach on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
        If kind is "GetterDeclaration" or kind is "SetterDeclaration", return cast property-beyond-reach on (statement).
        // A pipe of functions is the tasks slice; a pipe of programs is judged.
        If kind is "PipeExpression":
            If cast is-program-pipe on (statement), return "".
            Return "a pipe of functions".
        Done.
        If kind is "RepeatUntilStatement", return cast beyond-reach on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
        If kind is "ForEachStatement", return cast beyond-reach on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
        If kind is "BindStatement", return cast bind-beyond-reach on (statement).
        If kind is "UnmakerDeclaration", return cast beyond-reach on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
        If kind is "PullStatement", return cast beyond-reach on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)).
        If kind is "PullRabbitStatement", return cast beyond-reach on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)).
        If kind is "TryStatement":
            For each place in a series with (1, 2, 3), repeat:
                Define handler as cast field-of on (statement, place).
                If cast is-nothing on (handler) is false:
                    Define inner as cast beyond-reach on (handler).
                    If inner is not "", return inner.
                Done.
            Done.
            Return "".
        Done.
        For each known in a series with ("StateStatement", "BecomesStatement", "StopStatement", "SkipStatement",
                "ReturnStatement", "CastStatement", "PossessiveSetStatement", "RecordNamedSetStatement", "SuppressStatement",
                "MapSetStatement", "ExitStatement", "SeedChanceStatement", "MatrixSetStatement",
                "FileWriteStatement", "PathActionStatement", "CurrentDirectorySetStatement", "WriteToStreamStatement",
                "RunStatement", "AcknowledgeInterruptStatement",
                "SeriesInsertStatement", "SeriesSetStatement", "SeriesRemoveAtStatement", "SeriesRemoveValueStatement"), repeat:
            If kind is known, return "".
        Done.
        Return kind.
    Done.

    // ── The program ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// Top-level statements and those inside a `Pull` — what hoisting is transparent to.
    Bind series of node to hoistable, given (the node statements):
        Define found as a series of node.
        Cast gather-hoistable on (statements, found).
        Return found.
    Done.

    Bind void to gather-hoistable, given (the node statements, the series of node found):
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            Insert statement into found.
            If statement's kind is "PullStatement" or statement's kind is "PullRabbitStatement":
                Cast gather-hoistable on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), found).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The same, where an object definition is at the top level — the one place it can be judged.
    Bind text to program-beyond-reach, given (the node program):
        // Through Pull bodies statement by statement, since an object is judged there too.
        For each statement in cast hoistable on (program), repeat:
            Define inner as "".
            If statement's kind is "ObjectDefinition", the inner becomes cast object-beyond-reach on (statement).
            Otherwise if statement's kind is "InterfaceDefinition":
                The inner becomes cast interface-beyond-reach on (statement).
            Done.
            Otherwise if statement's kind is "BindStatement" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)) is false:
                The inner becomes cast unto-beyond-reach on (statement).
            Done.
            Otherwise if statement's kind is not "PullStatement" and statement's kind is not "PullRabbitStatement":
                The inner becomes cast statement-beyond-reach on (statement).
            Done.
            If inner is not "", return inner.
        Done.
        Return "".
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to check-program unto checker, given (the node program):
        Define reach as cast program-beyond-reach on (program).
        If reach is not "", return a failure (cast not-judged on (reach)).
        Cast check-versions on (program) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's hoist-interfaces on (program).
        Cast one's hoist-objects on (program) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's check-method-blanks or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's check-leftover-untos or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's hoist-functions on (program) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's hoist-makers on (program) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's resolve-types or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's hoist-shared-constants on (program) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's check-block on (program) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's check-pending-pulls or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// Every top-level `permanently` constant, registered before anything is checked — so a body
    /// may read one declared further down. A value that cannot be typed yet is left for the
    /// statement itself to refuse, in its own words.
    Bind void or failure to hoist-shared-constants unto checker, given (the node program):
        For each statement in cast hoistable on (program), repeat:
            If statement's kind is "DefineStatement" and cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)):
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                If (the entry for name in cast one's innermost) is void:
                    Define value-type as cast field-of on (statement, 7).
                    If cast is-nothing on (value-type):
                        The value-type becomes cast unknown-type.
                        Try to:
                            The value-type becomes cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)).
                        Done.
                        In case of failure:
                            Define said as the message of the failure.
                            If (the first 12 characters of said) is "unsupported\t", return a failure said.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                    If value-type's kind is not "none":
                        Cast one's bind-name on (name, a new binding {
                            the shape value-type,
                            the established-by cast field-of on (statement, 2),
                            the line cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)),
                            the permanent true, the module false, the depth 0, the parameter false }).
                        In one's hoisted-constants, the entry for name becomes true.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The statements of a block, in order — and after a guard that leaves when its condition
    /// holds, the rest of the block knows that condition was false.
    Bind void or failure to check-block unto checker, given (the node body):
        Define guarded as a series of text.
        Define before as a map from text to node.
        Define first-seen as a map from text to fact.
        For each statement in body's children, repeat:
            Cast one's check-statement on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            If statement's kind is "IfStatement" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)):
                Define arms as (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s children.
                If the number of arms is 1:
                    Define arm-body as cast field-of on (item 1 of arms, 2).
                    If cast definitely-returns on (arm-body) or cast leaves-the-block on (arm-body):
                        Define found as a map from text to node.
                        Define order as a series of text.
                        Cast one's guard-narrowings on (cast field-of on (item 1 of arms, 1), found, order).
                        For each name in order, repeat:
                            // Only the value from before this block's FIRST guard on the name is kept.
                            If (the entry for name in first-seen) is void:
                                In first-seen, the entry for name becomes true.
                                Define earlier as the entry for name in one's narrowed.
                                If earlier is not void, in before, the entry for name becomes earlier.
                            Done.
                            Insert name into guarded.
                            In one's narrowed, the entry for name becomes the entry for name in found but void is cast unknown-type.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        // Undone in reverse, so a narrowing never leaks into a sibling block.
        Define back as the number of guarded.
        While back is greater than 0, repeat:
            Define name as item back of guarded.
            Define earlier as the entry for name in before.
            If earlier is not void, in one's narrowed, the entry for name becomes earlier.
            Otherwise, cast one's forget-narrowing on (name).
            Decrement back by 1.
        Done.
    Done.

    Bind void to forget-narrowing unto checker, given (the text name):
        If (the entry for name in one's narrowed) is not void, remove name from one's narrowed.
    Done.

    /// What the NEGATION of a guard's condition proves — `x is void` means x is not, past it.
    Bind void to guard-narrowings unto checker, given (the node condition, the map from text to node found,
            the series of text order):
        // `x is a T`: past the guard, x is whatever else its declared union held.
        Define tested-name as cast type-tested on (condition).
        If tested-name is not "" and cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (condition, 3)) is false:
            Define declared as cast one's declared-type on (tested-name).
            If cast is-none on (declared), return.
            Define left-over as cast remove-from-union on (declared, cast field-of on (condition, 2)).
            If cast is-none on (left-over), return.
            In found, the entry for tested-name becomes left-over.
            Insert tested-name into order.
            Return.
        Done.
        If condition's kind is not "BinaryExpression", return.
        Define op as (cast field-of on (condition, 2))'s word.
        If op is "Or":
            Cast one's guard-narrowings on (cast field-of on (condition, 1), found, order).
            Cast one's guard-narrowings on (cast field-of on (condition, 3), found, order).
            Return.
        Done.
        If op is not "Equal" or (cast field-of on (condition, 3))'s kind is not "VoidLiteral", return.
        Define tested as cast field-of on (condition, 1).
        If tested's kind is not "VariableReference", return.
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tested, 1)).
        Define held as cast one's look-up on (name).
        If held is void, return.
        If held's shape's kind is not "VoidableType", return.
        In found, the entry for name becomes cast field-of on (held's shape, 1).
        Insert name into order.
    Done.

    /// Every path through these statements ends at a `Return` — C#'s `DefinitelyReturns`.
    Bind fact to definitely-returns, given (the node body):
        For each statement in body's children, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "ReturnStatement", return true.
            If statement's kind is "IfStatement" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) is false:
                Define every-arm as true.
                For each arm in (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s children, repeat:
                    If cast definitely-returns on (cast field-of on (arm, 2)) is false, the every-arm becomes false.
                Done.
                If every-arm and cast definitely-returns on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)), return true.
            Done.
            If statement's kind is "TryStatement" and cast definitely-returns on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)):
                Define all-handlers as true.
                For each place in a series with (2, 3), repeat:
                    Define handler as cast field-of on (statement, place).
                    If cast is-nothing on (handler) is false and cast definitely-returns on (handler) is false:
                        The all-handlers becomes false.
                    Done.
                Done.
                If all-handlers, return true.
            Done.
            // A judgement that reached here is total, so every arm returning is enough.
            If statement's kind is "JudgeStatement":
                Define every-arm as true.
                For each arm in (cast field-of on (statement, 2))'s children, repeat:
                    If cast definitely-returns on (cast field-of on (arm, 2)) is false, the every-arm becomes false.
                Done.
                Define rest as cast field-of on (statement, 3).
                If every-arm and (cast is-nothing on (rest) or cast definitely-returns on (rest)), return true.
            Done.
            If statement's kind is "PullStatement" or statement's kind is "PullRabbitStatement":
                If cast definitely-returns on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)), return true.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// The block is left without returning — a `Stop.`, `Skip.` or `Exit` among its own statements.
    Bind fact to leaves-the-block, given (the node body):
        For each statement in body's children, repeat:
            Define kind as statement's kind.
            If kind is "StopStatement" or kind is "SkipStatement" or kind is "ExitStatement", return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to check-statement unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define kind as statement's kind.
        If kind is "DefineStatement":
            Cast one's check-define on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "BecomesStatement":
            Cast one's check-becomes on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "StateStatement":
            Cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "IfStatement":
            Cast one's check-if on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "WhileStatement":
            Cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's enter-scope.
            Cast one's check-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's exit-scope.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "RepeatUntilStatement":
            Cast one's enter-scope.
            Cast one's check-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's exit-scope.
            Cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "ForEachStatement":
            Cast one's check-for-each on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "SeriesInsertStatement":
            Cast one's check-insert on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "SeriesSetStatement":
            Cast one's check-series-set on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "SeriesRemoveAtStatement":
            Cast one's check-remove-at on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "SeriesRemoveValueStatement":
            Cast one's check-remove-value on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "BindStatement":
            Cast one's check-bind-statement on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "UnmakerDeclaration":
            Cast one's check-unmaker on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "ReturnStatement":
            Cast one's check-return on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "CastStatement":
            Cast one's check-call on (statement, false) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "ObjectDefinition":
            Cast one's check-object-definition on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "PullStatement":
            Cast one's check-pull on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "PullRabbitStatement":
            Cast one's check-pull-rabbit on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "TryStatement":
            Cast one's check-try on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "SuppressStatement":
            Cast one's check-suppress on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "MapSetStatement":
            Cast one's check-map-set on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "ExitStatement":
            Cast one's check-exit on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        // An interface was gathered before anything was checked, and needs nothing more.
        Otherwise if kind is "PossessiveSetStatement":
            Cast one's check-possessive-set on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "RecordNamedSetStatement":
            Cast one's check-named-set on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "JudgeStatement":
            Cast one's check-judge on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "SeedChanceStatement":
            Cast one's check-seed on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "MatrixSetStatement":
            Cast one's check-matrix-set on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "FileWriteStatement":
            Cast one's check-file-write on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "PathActionStatement":
            Cast one's check-path-action on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "CurrentDirectorySetStatement":
            Cast one's check-directory-set on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "WithOpenStatement":
            Cast one's check-with-open on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "WriteToStreamStatement":
            Cast one's check-stream-write on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "RunStatement":
            Cast one's check-run-statement on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "PipeExpression":
            Cast one's check-pipe-statement on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        // A getter or setter written inside its object was checked with it.
        Otherwise if kind is "GetterDeclaration":
            If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)) is false:
                Cast one's check-getter-body on (statement, cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)), cast getter-row on (statement)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "SetterDeclaration":
            If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)) is false:
                Cast one's check-setter-body on (statement, cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)), cast setter-row on (statement)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    // ── If, and what its arms narrow ──────────────────────────────────────

    /// A narrowing held while one arm is checked, then put back as it was.
    Bind void to narrow unto checker, given (the text name, the node shape, the map from text to node saved):
        Define earlier as the entry for name in one's narrowed.
        If earlier is not void, in saved, the entry for name becomes earlier.
        In one's narrowed, the entry for name becomes shape.
    Done.

    Bind void to unnarrow unto checker, given (the text name, the map from text to node saved):
        Define earlier as the entry for name in saved.
        If earlier is not void, in one's narrowed, the entry for name becomes earlier.
        Otherwise, cast one's forget-narrowing on (name).
    Done.

    /// The name `<name> is void` or `<name> is not void` tests, when `op` is the test — or "".
    Bind text to void-tested, given (the node condition, the text op):
        If condition's kind is not "BinaryExpression", return "".
        If (cast field-of on (condition, 2))'s word is not op, return "".
        If (cast field-of on (condition, 3))'s kind is not "VoidLiteral", return "".
        Define tested as cast field-of on (condition, 1).
        If tested's kind is not "VariableReference", return "".
        Return cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tested, 1)).
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to check-if unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define arms as (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s children.
        // The Otherwise narrows by elimination while every arm tests the same name against a type.
        Define union-name as "".
        Define remaining-union as cast unknown-type.
        Define can-exhaust as true.
        // Or the other way round, after a lone arm testing that a name is NOT something.
        Define else-name as "".
        Define else-type as cast unknown-type.
        For each arm in arms, repeat:
            Define condition as cast field-of on (arm, 1).
            Cast one's infer on (condition) or pass the failure off.
            Define narrowed-name as "".
            Define narrowed-to as cast unknown-type.

            // `If x is not void:` — x is what it holds, inside the arm.
            Define present as cast void-tested on (condition, "NotEqual").
            Define absent as cast void-tested on (condition, "Equal").
            Define tested-name as cast type-tested on (condition).
            Define group as a series of node.
            Define group-name as cast group-tested on (condition, group).
            Define present-held as cast unknown-type.
            If present is not "", the present-held becomes cast one's declared-type on (present).
            Define absent-seen as cast unknown-type.
            If absent is not "" and the number of arms is 1:
                Define absent-held as cast one's look-up on (absent).
                If absent-held is not void:
                    The absent-seen becomes the entry for absent in one's narrowed but void is absent-held's shape.
                Done.
            Done.

            If present-held's kind is "VoidableType":
                The narrowed-name becomes present.
                The narrowed-to becomes cast field-of on (present-held, 1).
                The can-exhaust becomes false.
            Done.
            // `If x is void, … Otherwise, …` — a lone arm, and the Otherwise is where x is there.
            Otherwise if absent-seen's kind is "VoidableType":
                The else-name becomes absent.
                The else-type becomes cast field-of on (absent-seen, 1).
                The can-exhaust becomes false.
            Done.
            Otherwise if tested-name is not "":
                The narrowed-name becomes tested-name.
                Define tested-type as cast field-of on (condition, 2).
                If cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (condition, 3)) is false:
                    The narrowed-to becomes tested-type.
                    If can-exhaust:
                        If union-name is "":
                            The union-name becomes tested-name.
                            The remaining-union becomes cast one's declared-type on (tested-name).
                        Done.
                        Otherwise if union-name is not tested-name:
                            The can-exhaust becomes false.
                        Done.
                        If can-exhaust, the remaining-union becomes cast remove-from-union on (remaining-union, tested-type).
                    Done.
                Done.
                // Negated: the arm holds everything else, and a lone arm's Otherwise holds the type.
                Otherwise:
                    Define declared as cast one's declared-type on (tested-name).
                    The narrowed-to becomes cast remove-from-union on (declared, tested-type).
                    The can-exhaust becomes false.
                    If the number of arms is 1 and declared's kind is "UnionType":
                        For each one-case in cast union-cases on (declared), repeat:
                            If cast same-type on (one-case, tested-type):
                                The else-name becomes tested-name.
                                The else-type becomes tested-type.
                            Done.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            // A group narrows to the sub-union it names, and removes all of it for the Otherwise.
            Otherwise if group-name is not "":
                The narrowed-name becomes group-name.
                The narrowed-to becomes cast union-of on (group).
                If can-exhaust:
                    If union-name is "":
                        The union-name becomes group-name.
                        The remaining-union becomes cast one's declared-type on (group-name).
                    Done.
                    Otherwise if union-name is not group-name:
                        The can-exhaust becomes false.
                    Done.
                    If can-exhaust:
                        For each grouped-case in group, repeat:
                            If cast is-none on (remaining-union) is false and cast same-type on (remaining-union, grouped-case):
                                The remaining-union becomes cast unknown-type.
                            Done.
                            Otherwise, the remaining-union becomes cast remove-from-union on (remaining-union, grouped-case).
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                The can-exhaust becomes false.
            Done.

            Define saved as a map from text to node.
            Define narrowing as narrowed-name is not "" and cast is-none on (narrowed-to) is false.
            If narrowing, cast one's narrow on (narrowed-name, narrowed-to, saved).
            Cast one's enter-scope.
            Cast one's check-block on (cast field-of on (arm, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's exit-scope.
            If narrowing, cast one's unnarrow on (narrowed-name, saved).
        Done.
        Define otherwise-body as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        If cast is-nothing on (otherwise-body), return.
        Define saved as a map from text to node.
        If can-exhaust and union-name is not "" and cast is-none on (remaining-union) is false:
            The else-name becomes union-name.
            The else-type becomes remaining-union.
        Done.
        If cast is-none on (else-type), the else-name becomes "".
        If else-name is not "", cast one's narrow on (else-name, else-type, saved).
        Cast one's enter-scope.
        Cast one's check-block on (otherwise-body) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's exit-scope.
        If else-name is not "", cast one's unnarrow on (else-name, saved).
    Done.

    // ── Series ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind void or failure to check-for-each unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define looped as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
        Define looped-type as cast one's infer on (looped) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (looped-type), return.
        Define kind as looped-type's kind.
        If kind is "MapType":
            Define entry-type as cast plain-type on ("MappingType").
            Cast entry-type's add on (cast field-of on (looped-type, 1)).
            Cast entry-type's add on (cast field-of on (looped-type, 2)).
            Define map-iterator as "it".
            If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) is false:
                The map-iterator becomes cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
            Done.
            Cast one's enter-scope.
            Cast one's bind-name on (map-iterator, a new binding {
                the shape entry-type, the established-by looped, the line at-row, the permanent false,
                the module false, the depth 0, the parameter false }).
            Cast one's check-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's exit-scope.
            Return.
        Done.
        // A chase gives one-character texts; a set gives its elements.
        If kind is "ChaseType" or kind is "SetType":
            Define element-type as cast plain-type on ("TextType").
            If kind is "SetType", the element-type becomes cast field-of on (looped-type, 1).
            Define each-name as "it".
            If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) is false:
                The each-name becomes cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
            Done.
            Cast one's enter-scope.
            Cast one's bind-name on (each-name, a new binding {
                the shape element-type, the established-by looped, the line at-row, the permanent false,
                the module false, the depth 0, the parameter false }).
            Cast one's check-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's exit-scope.
            Return.
        Done.
        If kind is "StashType":
            Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("looping over a {kind}")).
        Done.
        If kind is not "SeriesType":
            If cast beyond-types on (looped-type), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("looping over a {kind}")).
            Define spoken as cast expression-words on (looped).
            Define plural as cast plural-words on (looped-type).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{spoken} holds {plural}", "It evaluates to {plural}, not a series",
                at-row, "loop over it as if it were a series",
                "Only series, maps and stashes can be looped over. Define a series if that's what you need.")).
        Done.
        Define iterator as "it".
        Define named as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        If cast is-nothing on (named) is false, the iterator becomes cast unquoted on (named).
        Define iterator-depth as one's rabbit-depth.
        If looped's kind is "VariableReference":
            Define source as cast one's look-up on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (looped, 1))).
            If source is not void, the iterator-depth becomes source's depth.
        Done.
        Cast one's enter-scope.
        Cast one's bind-name on (iterator, a new binding {
            the shape cast field-of on (looped-type, 1), the established-by looped, the line at-row, the permanent false,
            the module false, the depth iterator-depth, the parameter false }).
        Cast one's check-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's exit-scope.
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to check-insert unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define value as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define after-said as cast field-of on (statement, 3).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)).
        If cast is-nothing on (after-said) is false, cast check-index on (after-said, at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Define container as cast one's infer on (target) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (container), return.
        If container's kind is "SetType":
            Cast one's check-set-insert on (container, statement) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If container's kind is "ChaseType":
            Cast one's check-chase-insert on (value, target, at-row) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        Define spoken as cast expression-words on (target).
        If container's kind is not "SeriesType":
            If cast beyond-types on (container), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("inserting into a {container's kind}")).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{spoken} is not a series",
                "It evaluates to {cast plural-words on (container)}, which can't be inserted into",
                at-row, "insert into a non-series expression",
                "Only a series (like 'my-list' or 'one's cards') can be the target of 'Add ... to'.")).
        Done.
        Define element as cast field-of on (container, 1).
        Define given-type as cast one's infer on (value) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (given-type) is false and cast assignable on (element, given-type) is false:
            If cast beyond-types on (given-type) or cast beyond-types on (element), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("inserting another kind")).
            Define many as cast plural-words on (element).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{spoken} holds {many}",
                "It is a series of {many}, so it can only accept {many}",
                at-row, "add a {cast type-words on (given-type)} value to it",
                "Change the value to a {cast type-words on (element)}, or define a separate series that holds {cast plural-words on (given-type)}.")).
        Done.
        Cast one's check-region-store on (value, given-type, cast one's container-depth on (target), at-row,
            "add a region-scoped value to a series in a longer-lived region") or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to check-series-set unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define index-said as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
        If cast is-nothing on (index-said) is false, cast check-index on (index-said, at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Define container as cast one's infer on (target) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (container), return.
        Define spoken as cast expression-words on (target).
        If container's kind is "SeriesType":
            Define element as cast field-of on (container, 1).
            Define given-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-none on (given-type) is false and cast same-type on (given-type, element) is false:
                If cast beyond-types on (given-type) or cast beyond-types on (element), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("setting an item to another kind")).
                Define many as cast plural-words on (element).
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{spoken} holds {many}",
                    "It is a series of {many}, so its items can only be set to {many}",
                    at-row, "set an item to a {cast type-words on (given-type)} value",
                    "Change the new value to a {cast type-words on (element)}.")).
            Done.
            Cast one's check-region-store on (cast field-of on (statement, 3), given-type, cast one's container-depth on (target), at-row,
                "set an item in a series to a region-scoped value from a shorter-lived region") or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If container's kind is "ObjectType":
            If cast is-nothing on (index-said), return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'last' doesn't work on objects", "",
                at-row, "use 'last' on an object", "Use a position like 'the first of ...' or a field name like 'alice's name'.")).
            If index-said's kind is not "NumberLiteral", return.
            Define owner as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (container, 1)).
            Define positionals as a series of node.
            Cast one's gather-positionals on (owner, positionals).
            Define spot as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (index-said, 1)).
            Define whole as spot - (spot % 1).
            If whole is less than 1 or whole is greater than the number of positionals:
                Define said as "{spoken} has {the number of positionals} positional field(s) — there is no position {whole}".
                Define fix as "Positions run 1 through {the number of positionals}.".
                If the number of positionals is 0:
                    The said becomes "{spoken} has no positional fields".
                    The fix becomes "Object '{owner}' has no positional fields.".
                Done.
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (said, "", at-row, "set position {whole}", fix)).
            Done.
            Define wanted as item whole of positionals.
            Define given-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-none on (given-type) is false and cast same-type on (given-type, wanted) is false:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                    "position {whole} of {spoken} holds a {cast type-words on (wanted)}, not a {cast type-words on (given-type)}", "",
                    at-row, "set position {whole} to a {cast type-words on (given-type)}",
                    "Position {whole} has type {cast type-words on (wanted)}.")).
            Done.
            Return.
        Done.
        If container's kind is "RecordType":
            Cast one's check-record-item-set on (container, statement) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If container's kind is "ChaseType":
            Cast one's check-chase-text on (cast field-of on (statement, 3), target, at-row,
                "A chase is a buffer of characters, so a position can only be set to text",
                "set a position to a ", " value", "Convert it first: '<value> converted to text'.") or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If cast beyond-types on (container):
            Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("setting an item of a {container's kind}")).
        Done.
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{spoken} is not a series, object, or record",
            "It evaluates to {cast plural-words on (container)}, which can't have items assigned by position",
            at-row, "set an item in a non-series expression",
            "Only a series, object, or record can be the target of 'item N of ... becomes'.")).
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to check-remove-at unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define index-said as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
        If cast is-nothing on (index-said) is false, cast check-index on (index-said, at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Define container as cast one's infer on (target) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (container) or container's kind is "ChaseType" or container's kind is "SeriesType", return.
        If cast beyond-types on (container), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("removing from a {container's kind}")).
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{cast expression-words on (target)} is not a series",
            "It evaluates to {cast plural-words on (container)}, which can't have items removed by position",
            at-row, "remove an item from a non-series expression",
            "Only a series can be the target of 'Remove first/last/item N from'.")).
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to check-remove-value unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define value as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
        Define container as cast one's infer on (target) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (container), return.
        Define spoken as cast expression-words on (target).
        If container's kind is "MapType":
            Define removing as cast one's infer on (value) or pass the failure off.
            Define wanted-key as cast field-of on (container, 1).
            If cast is-none on (removing) is false and cast assignable on (wanted-key, removing) is false:
                If cast beyond-types on (removing), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a key of another kind")).
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{spoken} uses {cast type-words on (wanted-key)} keys",
                    "It is a map from {cast type-words on (wanted-key)} to {cast type-words on (cast field-of on (container, 2))}",
                    at-row, "remove using a {cast type-words on (removing)} key",
                    "Keys in this map are {cast plural-words on (wanted-key)}.")).
            Done.
            Return.
        Done.
        If container's kind is "ChaseType":
            Cast one's check-chase-text on (value, target, at-row,
                "A chase holds characters, so only a one-character text can be removed from it",
                "remove a ", " from it", "Remove a one-character text, as in 'Remove \",\" from <chase>'.") or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If container's kind is not "SeriesType":
            If cast beyond-types on (container), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("removing from a {container's kind}")).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{spoken} is not a series, chase or map",
                "It evaluates to {cast plural-words on (container)}, which can't have items removed",
                at-row, "remove from a non-series expression",
                "Only a series, a chase or a map can be the target of 'Remove ... from'.")).
        Done.
        Define element as cast field-of on (container, 1).
        Define given-type as cast one's infer on (value) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (given-type) is false and cast same-type on (given-type, element) is false:
            If cast beyond-types on (given-type) or cast beyond-types on (element), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("removing another kind")).
            Define many as cast plural-words on (element).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("{spoken} holds {many}",
                "It is a series of {many}, so only {many} can be removed from it",
                at-row, "remove a {cast type-words on (given-type)} value from it",
                "Make sure the value you're removing is a {cast type-words on (element)}.")).
        Done.
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to check-define unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
        Define value as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define permanent as cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
        Define shadowing as cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)).

        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)) is false:
            Cast one's check-resolves on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define value-type as cast one's infer on (value) or pass the failure off.
        If value-type's kind is "none":
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the type of the value for '{name}' can't be determined", "",
                at-row, "define a variable without a clear starting type",
                "Start with a literal value or a defined variable so the type is clear from the beginning.")).
        Done.

        // A hoisted shared constant reaching its own declaration is not a redefinition.
        Define reclaiming as false.
        If permanent and (the entry for name in one's hoisted-constants) is not void:
            The reclaiming becomes true.
            Remove name from one's hoisted-constants.
        Done.

        If (the entry for name in cast one's innermost) is not void and reclaiming is false:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is already defined in this scope", "",
                at-row, "define '{name}' again in the same block",
                "Each name can only be defined once per block. Use 'becomes' to reassign it, or choose a different name.")).
        Done.

        If reclaiming is false:
            Define outer as cast one's look-up-outer on (name).
            If outer is not void:
                If shadowing is false:
                    Define said as "It was defined on line {outer's line}".
                    If outer's line is 0:
                        The said becomes "'{name}' is built into every program — it is not written anywhere, so no line defines it".
                    Done.
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' already exists in an enclosing scope", said,
                        at-row, "declare '{name}' in this block without shadowing the outer one",
                        "To deliberately shadow it, write 'Define a shadow {name} as ...'.")).
                Done.
            Done.
            Otherwise if shadowing:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                    "'a shadow {name}' — there's nothing named '{name}' in an enclosing scope to shadow", "",
                    at-row, "shadow a name that doesn't exist in any enclosing scope",
                    "Remove 'a shadow' if you're just defining a new variable, or check the spelling.")).
            Done.
        Done.

        // An annotation is the binding's type; the value only has to fit into it.
        Define declared as cast field-of on (statement, 7).
        Define kept as value-type.
        If cast is-nothing on (declared) is false:
            If cast assignable on (declared, value-type) is false:
                If cast beyond-types on (value-type), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a {value-type's kind} into a declared type")).
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                    "'{name}' is declared as {cast type-words on (declared)}, but the value is a {cast type-words on (value-type)}", "",
                    at-row, "start '{name}' with a value that isn't a {cast type-words on (declared)}",
                    "Give it a {cast type-words on (declared)}, or change the declared type to match the value.")).
            Done.
            The kept becomes declared.
        Done.
        Cast one's bind-name on (name, a new binding {
            the shape kept, the established-by value, the line at-row, the permanent permanent, the module false,
            the depth one's rabbit-depth, the parameter false }).
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to check-becomes unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
        Define value as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
        // Reassigning ends whatever a test had narrowed the name to.
        Cast one's forget-narrowing on (name).
        Define existing as cast one's look-up on (name).
        If existing is void, return.

        If existing's permanent:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is permanent",
                "It was fixed with a value on line {existing's line} and can't be reassigned",
                at-row, "reassign it", "If it needs to change, define it without 'permanently'.")).
        Done.

        Define given-type as cast one's infer on (value) or pass the failure off.
        If given-type's kind is "none", return.

        If cast assignable on (existing's shape, given-type) is false:
            If cast beyond-types on (given-type) or cast beyond-types on (existing's shape):
                Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("reassigning a {existing's shape's kind}")).
            Done.
            If given-type's kind is "VoidableType":
                Define present as cast field-of on (given-type, 1).
                If cast assignable on (existing's shape, present):
                    Return a failure (cast void-misuse on (value,
                        "'{name}' holds {cast plural-words on (existing's shape)} that are there",
                        "give it a {cast type-words on (given-type)} value",
                        "'The {name} becomes {cast defaulted on (value, present)}'", at-row, "")).
                Done.
            Done.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' holds {cast plural-words on (existing's shape)}",
                "You set it to {cast expression-words on (existing's established-by)} on line {existing's line}, so it can only ever hold {cast plural-words on (existing's shape)}",
                at-row, "give it a {cast type-words on (given-type)} value",
                "Variables keep their type for life. If you need a {cast type-words on (given-type)} value here, define a new name for it instead.")).
        Done.
        Cast one's check-region-store on (value, given-type, existing's depth, at-row,
            "reassign '{name}' to a value from a shorter-lived region") or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// Does a value of type `source` fit where `target` is wanted — C#'s `IsAssignable`.
    Bind fact to assignable, given (the node target, the node source):
        If cast same-type on (target, source), return true.
        If target's kind is "VoidableType":
            Return cast assignable on (cast field-of on (target, 1), source) or source's kind is "VoidType".
        Done.
        If target's kind is "FailureType":
            Return cast assignable on (cast field-of on (target, 1), source) or source's kind is "FailureMarkerType".
        Done.
        If target's kind is "UnionType", return cast union-takes on (target, source).
        Return false.
    Done.

    // ── From outside ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// "ok", or the failure that says why not.
    Bind text or failure to checked, given (the node program, the series of node prelude):
        Define walker as a new checker {
            the scopes a series with (cast builtin-scope),
            the ended-names a map from text to number,
            the hoisted-constants a map from text to fact,
            the narrowed a map from text to node,
            the in-function false,
            the expected-returns a series with (cast unknown-type),
            the function-line 0,
            the hidden a map from text to fact,
            the defs a map from text to node,
            the def-order a series of text,
            the templates a map from text to fact,
            the bundled a map from text to fact,
            the type-scopes a series with (a map from text to node),
            the rabbit-depth 0,
            the nesting 0,
            the untos a map from text to node,
            the unto-order a series of text,
            the in-try false,
            the handled false,
            the in-exception-handler false,
            the interfaces a map from text to node,
            the checking-module "",
            the module-needs a map from text to series of text,
            the pending-pulls a series of pending-pull }.
        Cast walker's register-prelude on (prelude).
        Cast walker's check-program on (program) or pass the failure off.
        Return "ok".
    Done.
Done.
